  <section class="memo">
    <p class="memo-lead">
      I do compliance and risk for a living, which is one of the least fun sentences
      a person can say at a party — and yet somehow I chose this on purpose.
    </p>
    <p>
      What actually got me here: I care less about any one framework or checklist and
      more about the bigger picture — how security and risk actually show up inside a
      company, where the incentives get weird, and why the "correct" answer on paper
      doesn't always survive contact with an actual organization. Compliance is the
      day-to-day, but the part I find genuinely interesting is watching how risk
      decisions ripple through a business, not just whether a control box got checked.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm still early in this career, so treat my opinions accordingly — I'm in
      "collecting observations" mode more than "hot take" mode. This site is partly a
      record of that. The <a href="/labs">Labs section</a> is where I go break things
      and learn stuff outside the day job, mostly because staying technical still
      matters to me even in a role pulled more toward policy and process.
    </p>
  </section>

